      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.144,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "(gentle music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 5.16,
          "en": "-: Now let's talk about the filters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.16,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "So as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "the moment you add Spring Security in your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "basically all the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "it will first go to Spring Security",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 14.13,
          "en": "and then it verifies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 14.13,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "for all the authentication authorization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 16.98,
          "en": "If it is yes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 16.98,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "then only it will the request go to DispatchServlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 21.33,
          "en": "Now, what are the filters we have by default?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 21.33,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "Now, Spring Security works with multiple filters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "and we are not going to use all, but let's use a major one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 30.81,
          "en": "Now, how do you know which filters are applied?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "Now, if you see your console just after your password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "and you can see this, it says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 36.261,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "\"This generated password is for development use only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "Your security configuration must be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "before running the application production.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "That's right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "You don't want this password to be there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 46.83,
          "en": "for your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 48.93,
          "en": "For production, you have to use something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 48.93,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "Additionally, you only got one UsernamePassword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "Of course, your application will be having multiple users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "We have not seen how do we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "How do you have multiple usernames and passwords?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 58.68,
          "en": "We'll see that in the upcoming videos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "but we have to change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 62.25,
          "en": "Okay, let's look at the filters we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "And there's a concept of filter change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "Now this is not a new concept for Spring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "When you talk about servlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "we also got servlet filters there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "Now, just to give you a basic idea,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 74.13,
          "en": "let's say you're not using Spring Framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "you're using servlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 78.24,
          "en": "So the request goes from the client to servlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "And let's say if you want to add two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "your client will say, hey, I have these two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 84.943,
          "en": "two plus three added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 84.943,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "Servlet says, okay, two plus three is five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 88.35,
          "en": "Get the data back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 88.35,
          "end": 89.52,
          "en": "It works, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 89.52,
          "end": 92.31,
          "en": "But what if you want to check if the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "which you are getting from the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 95.46000000000001,
          "en": "are not negative values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 95.46000000000001,
          "end": 98.43,
          "en": "In that case, of course you can check the things in servlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "but the ideal cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "you can add a filter just before your servlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "So there's something servlet filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 107.67,
          "en": "and you can have this filter by checking the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 107.67,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "If it is a value is negative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 110.46000000000001,
          "en": "then you can respond back to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "by saying invalid request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 114.24000000000001,
          "en": "The servlet has no idea what happened,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "because who has done the work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 117.45,
          "en": "It's servlet filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 117.45,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "And not just one filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "You can have multiple filters there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "So one filter can call another filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 123.69,
          "en": "So maybe in the first filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 123.69,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "you're checking if the number is negative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 125.963,
          "en": "In the second filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 125.963,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "maybe you want to check the client location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 131.07,
          "en": "From where the client is accessing this data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 131.07,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "Maybe in the third filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "you want to check something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 135.9,
          "en": "So you can have multiple filters in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 135.9,
          "end": 137.7,
          "en": "And to connect all these filters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 137.7,
          "end": 139.41,
          "en": "we call them as FilterChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 139.41,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "So what happens is when you have three filters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "it's not like all the filters will execute at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 146.28,
          "en": "Basically it will go one by one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "So first filter, done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "It will send request to the next filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 151.53,
          "en": "Next filter will send request to third filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "And once all the filter done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "then the request goes to the actual servlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "Now the same concept, we have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 160.29,
          "en": "So when you implement Spring Security,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 163.17000000000002,
          "en": "it will have a lot of filters already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 163.17000000000002,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "So the moment you send a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.81,
          "en": "the request goes to the first filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 165.81,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "then second filter, then third filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 168.96,
          "en": "And you have all these filters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 168.96,
          "end": 171.32999999999998,
          "en": "and they are in a particular order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 171.32999999999998,
          "end": 173.94,
          "en": "And if you want to know which filter you can see in this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 173.94,
          "end": 175.787,
          "en": "it says \"DefaultSecurityFilterChain.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 176.85,
          "end": 178.02,
          "en": "So that's a FilterChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 181.29,
          "en": "And we got this filter, \"DisableEncoderUrlFilter.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 181.29,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "We got one more filter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 185.58,
          "en": "which is \"WebAsyncManagerIntegrationFilter.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 185.58,
          "end": 188.79,
          "en": "We got \"ContextHolderFilter\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "and the list goes on, they're huge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 194.91,
          "en": "So we got \"Cors\", we got \".csrf\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 194.91,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "And we'll talk about what is \"Cors\", what is \".csrf\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "in the upcoming videos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 201.87,
          "en": "We also got \".authentication\" filter for \".logout\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 201.87,
          "end": 204.27,
          "en": "We also got \".authentication\" filter for \"Login\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 204.27,
          "end": 207.63,
          "en": "For \"UsernamePasswordGeneratingFilter\" and the list goes on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 207.63,
          "end": 210.51,
          "en": "So all these filters are by default arranged",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 210.51,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "and they are in a particular order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "And they will execute in a particular order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "Can we change this order? Yes, we can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 217.74,
          "en": "But normally we do that? No.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "But yeah, we have the option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "You can change this order of the filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "but we have all these filters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 227.19,
          "en": "And let's try to understand the filters one by one, not all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 228.93,
          "en": "but we'll focus on some of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 228.93,
          "end": 230.16,
          "en": "But then we got the idea, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 230.16,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "So at least we are getting a login form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "And when you give the right credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "you will get the access for your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 238.41,
          "en": "And also, it's not like every time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "you want to access a resource,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 240.591,
          "en": "you have to log in once again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 240.591,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "It creates a session as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 244.5,
          "en": "So you can use that session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 244.5,
          "end": 247.89,
          "en": "and you can access the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 247.89,
          "end": 249.3,
          "en": "So that's it from this video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 249.3,
